Package: sampleone
Type: Package
Title: Survey Sampling Methods for Teaching and Practice
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Miguel Luiz", "de Almeida Pinto", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "phd20x@gmail.com"),
    person("Mariano", "Martinez Espinosa", role = "aut",
           comment = "Author of the source course material (course notes) this package implements")
    )
Description: Provides functions for planning, selecting, and estimating from
    surveys under the main probability sampling designs taught in
    introductory sampling courses: simple random sampling with and without
    replacement, stratified sampling (proportional, Neyman, and cost-based
    allocation), systematic sampling, one- and two-stage cluster sampling,
    and ratio and regression estimators. Functions accept a superset of the
    inputs a given formula requires and silently ignore arguments that are
    not needed for the selected computation. Each function returns a
    structured object with the point estimate, the associated variance and
    confidence interval, a step-by-step breakdown of the calculation, and a
    short pedagogical note suggesting related methods to explore, making the
    package suitable both for applied survey work and for classroom use.
    Methods follow Cochran (1977, ISBN:0-471-16240-X) and
    Bolfarine & Bussab (2005, ISBN:8521203675), among others referenced in
    each function's documentation.
